            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 75-year-old female patient, admitted on 31/08/1964 with acute lower abdominal pain and haemodynamic instability. Clinical examination and transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a tubal ectopic pregnancy with suspected rupture. Serum beta-hCG was markedly elevated. Given her unstable condition, emergency surgical intervention was performed. Laparoscopic salpingectomy was carried out successfully, with removal of the ectopic pregnancy from the affected fallopian tube. Intraoperative findings confirmed a ruptured tubal ectopic pregnancy. Blood loss was managed with intravenous fluid replacement. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and the patient was mobilised with physiotherapy support. She was discharged on 01/09/1964 in stable condition. Further gynaecological follow-up is recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
